(function(E){ const x = E["exam-06"] = E["exam-06"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x06-l4"] = {"id":"x06-l4","patterns":["L4-society","PARA-signpost"],"title":{"en":"Listening Part 4: a lecture on food trends","tr":"Listening Part 4: yemek eğilimleri üzerine bir ders","fa":"Listening Part 4: درسی درباره‌ی روندهای غذایی"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete notes on a lecture that follows a process step by step: use the signposts to keep your place, write one word in its exact form, and ignore the answer the lecturer corrects.","tr":"Bu derste bir süreci adım adım izleyen bir ders üzerine notları doldurmayı öğreneceksin: yerini korumak için yol işaretlerini kullanacak, tek kelimeyi tam biçimiyle yazacak ve öğretim görevlisinin düzelttiği cevabı göz ardı edeceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یادداشت‌های یک درس را که فرایندی را قدم به قدم دنبال می‌کند کامل کنی: از نشانه‌ها برای گم نکردن جایت استفاده کنی، یک کلمه را دقیقاً به همان شکل بنویسی و جوابی را که استاد اصلاح می‌کند نادیده بگیری."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Listening Part 4: a lecture on food trends","tr":"Listening Part 4: yemek eğilimleri üzerine bir ders","fa":"Listening Part 4: درسی درباره‌ی روندهای غذایی"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete notes on a lecture that follows a process step by step: use the signposts to keep your place, write one word in its exact form, and ignore the answer the lecturer corrects.","tr":"Bu derste bir süreci adım adım izleyen bir ders üzerine notları doldurmayı öğreneceksin: yerini korumak için yol işaretlerini kullanacak, tek kelimeyi tam biçimiyle yazacak ve öğretim görevlisinin düzelttiği cevabı göz ardı edeceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یادداشت‌های یک درس را که فرایندی را قدم به قدم دنبال می‌کند کامل کنی: از نشانه‌ها برای گم نکردن جایت استفاده کنی، یک کلمه را دقیقاً به همان شکل بنویسی و جوابی را که استاد اصلاح می‌کند نادیده بگیری."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"10"},{"label":{"en":"Speakers","tr":"Konuşan","fa":"گوینده"},"value":"1"},{"label":{"en":"Word limit","tr":"Kelime sınırı","fa":"سقف کلمه"},"value":{"en":"1 word","tr":"1 kelime","fa":"۱ کلمه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: how new snacks become popular","tr":"Bu sınav: yeni atıştırmalıklar nasıl popüler olur","fa":"این آزمون: تنقلات تازه چطور محبوب می‌شوند"},"intro":{"en":"Part 4 is always a lecture. Society, health and business topics come up often. When a lecture follows a process, the headings in the notes are the stages, and the lecturer announces each new stage.","tr":"Part 4 her zaman bir derstir. Toplum, sağlık ve iş konuları sık çıkar. Ders bir süreci izlediğinde notlardaki başlıklar aşamalardır ve öğretim görevlisi her yeni aşamayı duyurur.","fa":"Part 4 همیشه یک درس است. موضوع‌های جامعه، سلامت و کسب‌وکار زیاد می‌آیند. وقتی درس یک فرایند را دنبال می‌کند، عنوان‌های یادداشت همان مرحله‌ها هستند و استاد هر مرحله‌ی تازه را اعلام می‌کند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x06-l4-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["L4-society","PARA-signpost"],"often":{"pattern":"L4-society","n":10,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 10 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 10’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۰ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A lecture on how new foods become popular","tr":"Yeni yiyeceklerin nasıl popüler olduğuna dair bir ders","fa":"درسی درباره‌ی اینکه خوراکی‌های تازه چطور محبوب می‌شوند"},"asks":{"en":"A lecturer follows a process from start to finish: where new products come from, how they are tested, how they spread online, what happens in supermarkets and why many fail. The notes follow these stages.","tr":"Bir öğretim görevlisi bir süreci baştan sona izliyor: yeni ürünlerin nereden geldiği, nasıl test edildiği, internette nasıl yayıldığı, süpermarketlerde ne olduğu ve birçoğunun neden başarısız olduğu. Notlar bu aşamaları izler.","fa":"یک استاد فرایندی را از اول تا آخر دنبال می‌کند: محصولات تازه از کجا می‌آیند، چطور آزمایش می‌شوند، چطور در اینترنت پخش می‌شوند، در سوپرمارکت چه اتفاقی می‌افتد و چرا خیلی‌هایشان شکست می‌خورند. یادداشت‌ها همین مرحله‌ها را دنبال می‌کنند."},"fields":["Origins","Testing","Social media","Supermarkets","Why products fail"],"words":[{"a":"small producers","b":"a family business / a single cook","tr":"küçük üreticiler","fa":"تولیدکننده‌های کوچک"},{"a":"launch","b":"bring out / put on sale","tr":"piyasaya sürmek","fa":"عرضه کردن"},{"a":"tasting panel","b":"a group of people paid to try samples","tr":"tadım paneli","fa":"گروه چشنده"},{"a":"texture","b":"how it feels in the mouth / crunch","tr":"doku","fa":"بافت"},{"a":"go viral","b":"be shared very widely online","tr":"viral olmak","fa":"در فضای مجازی دست‌به‌دست شدن"},{"a":"on impulse","b":"without planning to buy","tr":"anlık karar ile","fa":"بی‌برنامه، هوسی"},{"a":"stock","b":"agree to sell","tr":"satışa koymak","fa":"در فروشگاه عرضه کردن"},{"a":"fees","b":"money charged for a service","tr":"ücretler","fa":"هزینه‌ها، کارمزد"},{"a":"familiar","b":"what people already know","tr":"tanıdık","fa":"آشنا"},{"a":"let’s turn to","b":"next / now let’s look at","tr":"şimdi ... geçelim","fa":"حالا برویم سراغ"},{"a":"finally","b":"my last point / to sum up","tr":"son olarak","fa":"در آخر"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"You’d expect X... but what matters most is Y.\" The expected word is said first. Write the word that comes after but or in fact.","tr":"\"X beklersiniz... ama en önemlisi Y.\" Beklenen kelime önce söylenir. But ya da in fact’ten sonra gelen kelimeyi yaz.","fa":"«انتظار X را داری... اما مهم‌ترین چیز Y است». کلمه‌ی قابل انتظار اول گفته می‌شود. کلمه‌ای را بنویس که بعد از but یا in fact می‌آید."},{"en":"Plural endings: the lecturer may say \"reactions\" or \"colours\". The s is part of the answer.","tr":"Çoğul ekleri: öğretim görevlisi \"reactions\" ya da \"colours\" diyebilir. s cevabın parçasıdır.","fa":"نشانه‌ی جمع: ممکن است استاد «reactions» یا «colours» بگوید. s جزو جواب است."},{"en":"ONE WORD ONLY: if you hear \"the big supermarket chains\", the gap needs one of those words, chosen by the words printed around it.","tr":"ONE WORD ONLY: \"the big supermarket chains\" duyarsan, boşluk bu kelimelerden birini ister; etrafında yazılı kelimeler hangisini seçeceğini söyler.","fa":"ONE WORD ONLY: اگر «the big supermarket chains» را بشنوی، جای خالی یکی از این کلمه‌ها را می‌خواهد و کلمه‌های چاپ‌شده‌ی اطرافش می‌گویند کدام."}],"example":{"lines":[["Lecturer","You might think the price matters most to shoppers. In fact, the packaging is what they notice first."]],"item":"Shoppers first notice the ___","answer":"packaging","why":{"en":"Price is the expected answer; \"in fact\" introduces the right one: packaging.","tr":"Fiyat beklenen cevap; \"in fact\" doğrusunu getiriyor: packaging.","fa":"قیمت جواب قابل انتظار است؛ «in fact» جواب درست را می‌آورد: packaging."}}},{"id":"L4-society","ctx":["L4-society"],"title":{"en":"Society, health and business","tr":"Toplum, sağlık ve iş dünyası","fa":"جامعه، سلامت و کسب‌وکار"},"asks":{"en":"A presenter reports research on people: health, memory, music therapy, food trends, design for everyone or the workplace. The notes cover the problem, the study, the findings and what should change.","tr":"Bir sunucu insanlarla ilgili bir araştırmayı aktarır: sağlık, hafıza, müzik terapisi, yiyecek trendleri, herkes için tasarım ya da iş yeri. Notlar sorunu, çalışmayı, bulguları ve neyin değişmesi gerektiğini kapsar.","fa":"یک ارائه‌دهنده پژوهشی درباره‌ی آدم‌ها را گزارش می‌کند: سلامت، حافظه، موسیقی‌درمانی، روندهای غذایی، طراحی برای همه یا محیط کار. یادداشت‌ها مسئله، پژوهش، یافته‌ها و تغییرات لازم را پوشش می‌دهند."},"fields":["Background","Method","Participants","Findings","Benefits","Limitations","Recommendations"],"words":[{"a":"participants","b":"the people in the study / volunteers","tr":"katılımcılar","fa":"شرکت‌کننده‌ها"},{"a":"findings","b":"what the study showed","tr":"bulgular","fa":"یافته‌ها"},{"a":"therapy","b":"treatment","tr":"terapi","fa":"درمان"},{"a":"patients","b":"people in hospital","tr":"hastalar","fa":"بیماران"},{"a":"recovery","b":"getting better after an illness","tr":"iyileşme","fa":"بهبودی"},{"a":"stress","b":"feeling under pressure","tr":"stres","fa":"استرس"},{"a":"consumers","b":"shoppers / people who buy","tr":"tüketiciler","fa":"مصرف‌کننده‌ها"},{"a":"trend","b":"what's becoming popular","tr":"eğilim","fa":"روند"},{"a":"productivity","b":"how much work gets done","tr":"verimlilik","fa":"بهره‌وری"},{"a":"accessible","b":"easy for everyone to use","tr":"erişilebilir","fa":"قابل دسترس"},{"a":"elderly","b":"older people","tr":"yaşlılar","fa":"سالمندان"},{"a":"limitation","b":"what the study didn't look at","tr":"sınırlılık","fa":"محدودیت"},{"a":"recommend","b":"the speaker suggests","tr":"önermek","fa":"توصیه کردن"}],"traps":[{"en":"Check the group: \"older patients\" and \"all patients\" can have different answers.","tr":"Grubu kontrol et: \"yaşlı hastalar\" ile \"bütün hastalar\" farklı cevaplara sahip olabilir.","fa":"گروه را چک کن: «بیماران مسن» و «همه‌ی بیماران» ممکن است جواب‌های متفاوتی داشته باشند."},{"en":"Findings and limitations sound alike: \"the study showed X, but it didn’t look at Y\". Read the heading.","tr":"Bulgular ve sınırlılıklar birbirine benzer: \"çalışma X’i gösterdi ama Y’ye bakmadı\". Başlığı oku.","fa":"یافته‌ها و محدودیت‌ها شبیه هم‌اند: «پژوهش X را نشان داد، ولی Y را بررسی نکرد». عنوان را بخوان."}],"example":{"lines":[["Lecturer","Patients who listened to music before surgery needed less medication afterwards."],["Lecturer","Interestingly, the type of music made no difference."],["Lecturer","What mattered was that patients chose it themselves."]],"item":"Key factor: patients ___ the music themselves   (ONE WORD ONLY)","answer":"chose","why":{"en":"The type of music \"made no difference\". \"What mattered\" introduces the answer: chose.","tr":"Müziğin türü \"fark yaratmadı\". \"What mattered\" cevabı getiriyor: chose.","fa":"نوع موسیقی «فرقی نداشت». «What mattered» جواب را می‌آورد: chose."}},"general":true,"patterns":["L4-society"],"often":{"pattern":"L4-society","n":10,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 10 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 10’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۰ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Ten notes, no break","tr":"On not, ara yok","fa":"ده یادداشت، بدون وقفه"},"body":{"en":"Questions 31-40 are notes under five headings. You have 45 seconds to read them, then the lecture plays to the end without a pause. Limit: ONE WORD ONLY. Two or three answers usually come from each stage of the lecture.","tr":"Soru 31-40 beş başlık altındaki notlardır. Okumak için 45 saniyen var, sonra ders duraklamadan sonuna kadar çalar. Sınır: ONE WORD ONLY. Genelde dersin her aşamasından iki üç cevap gelir.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۳۱ تا ۴۰ یادداشت‌هایی زیر پنج عنوان‌اند. ۴۵ ثانیه برای خواندنشان داری و بعد درس بدون مکث تا آخر پخش می‌شود. سقف: ONE WORD ONLY. معمولاً از هر مرحله‌ی درس دو سه جواب می‌آید."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Follow the stages","tr":"Aşamaları takip et","fa":"مرحله‌ها را دنبال کن"},"steps":[{"en":"Read the headings and turn each into a question: Where from? How tested? How shared?","tr":"Başlıkları oku ve her birini bir soruya çevir: Nereden? Nasıl test edildi? Nasıl yayıldı?","fa":"عنوان‌ها را بخوان و هر کدام را به سؤال تبدیل کن: از کجا؟ چطور آزمایش شد؟ چطور پخش شد؟"},{"en":"Mark the signposts as you hear them: let’s begin with, the next stage, let’s turn to, finally.","tr":"Yol işaretlerini duydukça işaretle: let’s begin with, the next stage, let’s turn to, finally.","fa":"نشانه‌ها را وقتی می‌شنوی علامت بزن: let’s begin with، the next stage، let’s turn to، finally."},{"en":"Write the word you hear, with its ending; if you miss one, move straight to the next gap.","tr":"Duyduğun kelimeyi ekiyle birlikte yaz; birini kaçırırsan hemen bir sonraki boşluğa geç.","fa":"کلمه‌ای را که می‌شنوی با پسوندش بنویس؛ اگر یکی را از دست دادی، فوراً برو سراغ جای خالی بعدی."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"The expected answer comes first","tr":"Beklenen cevap önce gelir","fa":"جواب قابل انتظار اول می‌آید"},"body":{"en":"Lecturers often say what most people would expect, then correct it: \"You’d expect the flavour... but what testers react to most strongly is...\" Both words fit the gap, so the signal word decides. Write the second one.","tr":"Öğretim görevlileri çoğu zaman insanların çoğunun bekleyeceği şeyi söyler, sonra düzeltir: \"Tadı beklersiniz... ama testçilerin en güçlü tepki verdiği şey...\" İki kelime de boşluğa uyar, bu yüzden işaret kelimesi karar verir. İkincisini yaz.","fa":"استادها اغلب چیزی را می‌گویند که بیشتر آدم‌ها انتظارش را دارند و بعد اصلاحش می‌کنند: «انتظار داری طعم باشد... اما چیزی که آزمایش‌کننده‌ها بیشتر از همه به آن واکنش نشان می‌دهند...». هر دو کلمه در جای خالی جا می‌شوند، پس کلمه‌ی نشانه تصمیم می‌گیرد. دومی را بنویس."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One note, step by step","tr":"Bir not, adım adım","fa":"یک یادداشت، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the notes below. Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.","item":"Cafés · Most new customers come because of ___","lines":[["Lecturer","Let’s turn to cafés. Owners spend a lot on advertising, but most new customers say they came because of recommendations from friends."]],"answer":"recommendations","walk":[{"en":"\"Let’s turn to cafés\" tells you that you have reached the Cafés heading.","tr":"\"Let’s turn to cafés\" Cafés başlığına geldiğini söylüyor.","fa":"«Let’s turn to cafés» می‌گوید به عنوان Cafés رسیده‌ای."},{"en":"Advertising is mentioned, but \"but most new customers say\" brings the answer.","tr":"Reklamdan söz ediliyor ama \"ama yeni müşterilerin çoğu diyor ki\" cevabı getiriyor.","fa":"از تبلیغات حرف زده می‌شود، اما «اما بیشتر مشتری‌های تازه می‌گویند» جواب را می‌آورد."},{"en":"Write recommendations, with the s. \"from friends\" is extra.","tr":"recommendations’ı s’siyle yaz. \"from friends\" fazladan.","fa":"recommendations را با s بنویس. «from friends» اضافه است."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Note: \"The most popular flavour among children: ___ (ONE WORD ONLY)\". You hear: \"You’d think it would be chocolate. Actually it’s strawberry, by a long way.\" What do you write?","options":["chocolate","strawberry","strawberry chocolate"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Chocolate is the expected answer; \"actually\" gives the right one: strawberry.","tr":"Çikolata beklenen cevap; \"actually\" doğrusunu veriyor: strawberry.","fa":"شکلات جواب قابل انتظار است؛ «actually» جواب درست را می‌دهد: strawberry."}},"remember":{"en":"Use the signposts to stay on the right heading, and write the word that comes after but or in fact.","tr":"Doğru başlıkta kalmak için yol işaretlerini kullan ve but ya da in fact’ten sonra gelen kelimeyi yaz.","fa":"از نشانه‌ها استفاده کن تا روی عنوان درست بمانی و کلمه‌ای را بنویس که بعد از but یا in fact می‌آید."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x06-l4-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-l4"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"listening","part":"Listening Part 4","title":{"en":"How new snack foods become popular","tr":"Yeni atıştırmalıklar nasıl popüler olur","fa":"تنقلات تازه چطور محبوب می‌شوند"},"timed":8,"ctx":["L4-society"],"script":[{"who":"Lecturer","line":"Good morning, everyone. In this part of the course on food and society, we're looking at how new products reach our shelves. Today I want to take one very ordinary category, snack foods, and ask a simple question: how does a new snack go from an idea to something millions of people buy without thinking? I'll follow the process in order, from the first idea to the supermarket, and then look at why most new products fail."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"Let's begin with where the ideas come from. You might imagine teams of scientists in the laboratories of huge food companies. In fact, most successful new snacks start with small independent producers, often a family business or a single cook selling at markets. The big companies tend to be cautious. They wait, watch what sells, and then either copy the product or buy the business. And where do the small producers get their ideas? Very often from street food in other countries. Something that has been eaten for generations in one place can seem completely new in another. Roasted chickpeas, seaweed crisps and spicy dried fruit all followed this path, moving from market stalls to supermarket shelves in only a few years."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"The next stage is testing. Before a product is launched widely, it's tested on panels of volunteers, who are paid a small fee to taste samples and fill in a detailed questionnaire. Now, you'd expect the most important factor to be flavour, and of course flavour matters. But what testers react to most strongly is texture. A crisp that doesn't make the right sound when you bite it will fail, however good it tastes. Some companies even record the noise of people eating in special sound-proof rooms. Testers are also asked how likely they would be to buy the product again, which turns out to be a much better guide to future sales than whether they simply say they liked it."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"Let's turn to the role of social media, which has changed this industry enormously in the last ten years, perhaps more than any other single factor. A small producer no longer needs a big advertising budget. What spreads a new snack is short videos of people trying it for the first time. It's their reactions that viewers enjoy: surprise, disgust, delight. Researchers who have studied thousands of these videos found one feature that seems to predict success. Products with unusual colours are shared far more often than ordinary-looking ones, even when the flavour is quite normal. A bright blue snack is simply more interesting to film. Companies have noticed this, of course, and some now design the appearance of a product before they have even decided what it should taste like."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"But online fame only gets a product so far. For most snacks, real success still means getting into the big supermarkets, so let's look at how they work. When a supermarket agrees to stock a new product, it usually places it near the checkouts for the first few weeks, because that's where people buy on impulse while they're waiting in the queue. Later it moves to the main shelves, and here the competition is fierce. Supermarkets charge producers fees for the best positions, at eye level or at the end of an aisle. For a small company, these fees can be the biggest single cost of launching a product. If sales are slow in the first few months, the supermarket can remove the product from its shelves, and many small producers never recover from that."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"Finally, why do so many new snacks fail? Industry estimates suggest that the majority disappear within two years. One reason is price. People are happy to try something new once, but if it costs much more than familiar snacks, they soon go back to what they know. Another is health claims. Many new products are marketed as healthy alternatives, but in most countries such claims must now be supported by evidence, and a product that can't prove what it promises may have to change its packaging or leave the market altogether. And some products simply arrive at the wrong moment, when shoppers are cutting back and are less willing to take a risk on something they have never tried."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"So, to sum up, and this is the main point I want you to take away from today: new snacks usually begin with small producers, succeed or fail on texture in testing, spread online through people's reactions, and then face the hard economics of supermarket shelves. In next week's session, we'll apply the same questions to drinks, where the story is surprisingly different."}],"notes":{"title":"New snack foods: from idea to supermarket","headings":["Origins","Testing","Social media","Supermarkets","Why products fail"],"extra":["Origins · large companies often copy successful products or buy the business","Why products fail · most disappear within two years"]},"groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 31-40. Complete the notes below. Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.","qtype":"note","questions":[{"n":31,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Origins · most successful new snacks start with small ___ producers","accept":["independent"],"limit":1,"evidence":"start with small independent producers","why":{"en":"Not big companies’ laboratories: \"small independent producers\". \"small\" and \"producers\" are printed.","tr":"Büyük şirketlerin laboratuvarları değil: \"küçük bağımsız üreticiler\". \"small\" ve \"producers\" yazılı.","fa":"نه آزمایشگاه شرکت‌های بزرگ: «تولیدکننده‌های کوچکِ مستقل». «small» و «producers» چاپ شده‌اند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-limit"]},{"n":32,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Origins · ideas often come from street food in other ___","accept":["countries"],"limit":1,"evidence":"street food in other countries","why":{"en":"\"Very often from street food in other countries.\" Plural.","tr":"\"Çoğu zaman başka ülkelerdeki sokak yemeklerinden.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«خیلی وقت‌ها از غذای خیابانیِ کشورهای دیگر». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":33,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Testing · samples are tasted by paid ___","accept":["volunteers"],"limit":1,"evidence":"tested on panels of volunteers","why":{"en":"\"Panels of volunteers, who are paid a small fee to taste samples.\"","tr":"\"Numuneleri tatmak için küçük bir ücret alan gönüllü panelleri.\"","fa":"«گروه‌هایی از داوطلب‌ها که برای چشیدن نمونه‌ها پول کمی می‌گیرند»."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":34,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Testing · testers react most strongly to the ___","accept":["texture"],"limit":1,"evidence":"what testers react to most strongly is texture","why":{"en":"Flavour \"matters\", but \"what testers react to most strongly is texture\".","tr":"Tat \"önemli\" ama \"testçilerin en güçlü tepki verdiği şey doku\".","fa":"طعم «مهم است»، اما «چیزی که آزمایش‌کننده‌ها بیشتر از همه به آن واکنش نشان می‌دهند بافت است»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":35,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Social media · videos of people’s ___ when trying a snack","accept":["reactions"],"limit":1,"evidence":"It's their reactions that viewers enjoy","why":{"en":"\"It’s their reactions that viewers enjoy: surprise, disgust, delight.\" Plural.","tr":"\"İzleyicilerin hoşlandığı şey onların tepkileri: şaşkınlık, tiksinti, sevinç.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«چیزی که بیننده‌ها از آن لذت می‌برند واکنش‌هایشان است: تعجب، چندش، شوق». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":36,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Social media · snacks with unusual ___ are shared more often","accept":["colours"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Products with unusual colours are shared far more often","why":{"en":"\"Products with unusual colours are shared far more often.\"","tr":"\"Alışılmadık renkteki ürünler çok daha sık paylaşılıyor.\"","fa":"«محصولاتی با رنگ‌های غیرعادی خیلی بیشتر به اشتراک گذاشته می‌شوند»."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":37,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Supermarkets · new products are first placed near the ___","accept":["checkouts"],"limit":1,"evidence":"it usually places it near the checkouts","why":{"en":"\"Near the checkouts for the first few weeks\", where people buy on impulse.","tr":"\"İlk birkaç hafta kasaların yakınında\", insanların anlık alışveriş yaptığı yerde.","fa":"«چند هفته‌ی اول نزدیک صندوق‌ها»، جایی که مردم هوسی خرید می‌کنند."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":38,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Supermarkets · producers pay fees for the best ___","accept":["positions"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Supermarkets charge producers fees for the best positions","why":{"en":"\"Fees for the best positions, at eye level or at the end of an aisle.\"","tr":"\"Göz hizasında ya da reyon sonunda en iyi yerler için ücretler.\"","fa":"«کارمزد برای بهترین جاها، هم‌سطح چشم یا آخر راهرو»."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":39,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Why products fail · they cost much more than ___ snacks","accept":["familiar"],"limit":1,"evidence":"if it costs much more than familiar snacks","why":{"en":"\"If it costs much more than familiar snacks, they soon go back to what they know.\"","tr":"\"Tanıdık atıştırmalıklardan çok daha pahalıysa, kısa sürede bildiklerine dönerler.\"","fa":"«اگر خیلی گران‌تر از تنقلات آشنا باشد، زود به همان چیزی که می‌شناسند برمی‌گردند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":40,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Why products fail · health claims must be supported by ___","accept":["evidence"],"limit":1,"evidence":"such claims must now be supported by evidence","why":{"en":"\"Such claims must now be supported by evidence.\" One word, no plural.","tr":"\"Bu tür iddialar artık kanıtla desteklenmeli.\" Tek kelime, çoğul değil.","fa":"«این ادعاها حالا باید با شواهد پشتیبانی شوند». یک کلمه، بدون جمع."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]}],"audio":{"voices":{"Announcer":{"accent":"British (standard Southern)","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_george"},"role":"Recorded rubric"},"Lecturer":{"accent":"Australian","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_lewis","fallback":true,"note":"Australian wanted; no free Australian voice yet"},"role":"Lecturer"}},"sequence":[{"type":"announcer","text":"Part 4. You will hear a lecture about how new snack foods become popular. First, you have some time to look at Questions 31 to 40."},{"type":"pause","seconds":45,"note":"reading time, Questions 31-40"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen carefully and answer Questions 31 to 40."},{"type":"sfx","note":"lecture-room acoustics: slight room reverb; 1.5 s between paragraphs"},{"type":"lines","from":0,"to":6},{"type":"announcer","text":"That is the end of Part 4. You now have two minutes to check your answers.","after":120}]},"id":"c-x06-l4-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-l4"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Shoppers buy sweets near the till on impulse.\" On impulse means...","options":["suddenly, without planning to","after comparing prices","because they need them"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"An impulse buy is not planned.","tr":"Anlık alışveriş planlanmamıştır.","fa":"خرید هوسی از قبل برنامه‌ریزی نشده."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":2,"prompt":"Note: \"Claims must be ___ by research\". Which words in a lecture give the answer?","options":["claims are popular with researchers","research is expensive","claims have to be backed up by research"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Backed up = supported. The verb in the gap is supported or backed.","tr":"Backed up = desteklenmiş. Boşluktaki fiil supported ya da backed.","fa":"backed up یعنی supported. فعل جای خالی supported یا backed است."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"The lecturer says \"Let’s turn to supermarkets.\" What should you do?","options":["Go back to the first heading","Move your eyes to the Supermarkets heading","Stop writing until the end"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A signpost names the next stage; follow it in the notes.","tr":"Yol işareti bir sonraki aşamayı adlandırır; notlarda onu takip et.","fa":"نشانه اسم مرحله‌ی بعد را می‌گوید؛ در یادداشت‌ها دنبالش کن."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Note: \"Customers care most about ___ (ONE WORD ONLY)\". You hear: \"You’d expect them to care about price, but actually freshness comes first.\" What do you write?","options":["freshness","price","price and freshness"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Price is the expected answer; \"actually\" gives the right one.","tr":"Fiyat beklenen cevap; \"actually\" doğrusunu veriyor.","fa":"قیمت جواب قابل انتظار است؛ «actually» جواب درست را می‌دهد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":1,"prompt":"Note: \"A ___ explains the rules (ONE WORD ONLY)\". You hear: \"There’s a short leaflet that explains all the rules.\" What do you write?","options":["short leaflet","leaflets","leaflet"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"One word only, and the singular you hear: leaflet.","tr":"Yalnızca bir kelime ve duyduğun tekil biçim: leaflet.","fa":"فقط یک کلمه، به همان شکل مفردی که می‌شنوی: leaflet."}}],"id":"c-x06-l4-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-l4"}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
